  "markdown_content": "Hindustan Unilever Limited (HUL), the owner of the Lakme brand, made a formal commitment to the Delhi High Court on Thursday regarding the modification of their advertising content. The company stated it would withdraw and republish its advertisements after removing all references that allegedly disparage the Derma Co brand, owned by Honasa Consumer Limited.\\n\\nThe decision comes amid growing concerns about comparative advertising and brand disparagement in the cosmetics industry. The case highlights the legal boundaries companies must observe when creating competitive marketing campaigns.",
